{
  "info": {
    "title": "Ozone Connect - Bank Service Initiation APIs",
    "description": "This document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html)\nfor Bank Service Initiation APIs for Ozone Connect.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by a Financial Institution so that Ozone can deliver Service Initiation capabilities to TPPs\n\n### Versioning\n\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where:\n\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n### v2.2.1\n* Added new version compatible with v2.2 of standards\n* Changed every date-time field to reference the shared `AEDateTime` Schema Object. `AEDateTime` states that a\n  date-time value identifies an instant, that the offset is part of the value and must be applied by the\n  recipient, and that two encodings of the same instant are equivalent and must behave identically. It carries\n  a `pattern` requiring an offset and forbidding `-00:00`; all other offsets remain conformant. Each field\n  description now states only what is specific to that field. Per OFP-014.\n\n### v2.1.8\n\n* Added a character-set `pattern` (`^[A-Za-z0-9 \\/?:().,'+-]+$`, the ISO 20022 / SWIFT \"x\" set) to the\n  free-text Creditor and Debtor references (`AECreditorReference` / `AEDebtorReference`), so every LFI\n  knows exactly which characters it must accept and store. Length (`minLength 1` / `maxLength 35`) is\n  unchanged. Per OFP-003.\n\n\n### v2.1.7\n\n* Restructured the international Creditor PII (`PersonalIdentifiableInformation.Initiation.Creditor`) for\n  SWIFT SR2026: the Creditor party is now a `oneOf` of Individual and Organization variants, discriminated\n  by `IdentityType`.\n\n\n* The Individual variant carries object-valued `FirstName` / `MiddleName` / `LastName` (`en` / `ar` / `ls`),\n  `RelationshipToSender`, `DateOfBirth`, `Occupation`, `Nationality`, `Gender`, `CountryOfBirth`,\n  `SourceOfIncome`, `SourceOfFunds`, and `Evidence`. The Organization variant carries `AnyBIC`, `LEI`, and\n  `Identification` + `SchemeName`. Both variants share `MobileNumber` / `Email` and an object-valued `Name`\n  (`en` / `ar` / `ls`).\n\n\n* Added SWIFT SR2026 fields to the international `PostalAddress` (`PostCode`, `Room`, `Department`,\n  `SubDepartment`, `TownLocationName`, and now-mandatory `TownName`). It is now a single\n  `AEInternationalAddress` schema shared by both the Creditor and the Creditor Agent (the Creditor Agent\n  previously used the legacy `AEAddress`).\n\n\n* Added a `CreditorAgent.Branch` object and `CreditorAccount.AccountType` (Savings / Current / Checking /\n  Prepaid). Domestic Creditor schemas are unchanged.\n\n\n### v2.1.6\n\n* Aligned the `Risk` object with Standards: tightened `AERisk` and its descendants with `additionalProperties: false` throughout, matching the strictness on the Standards PAR side. `SupplementaryData` blocks remain open extension points and `AEAccountTypeCode` already carried `Retail / SME / Corporate`.\n\n### v2.1.5\n\n* Changed the `UAEAccountInformationAPI.AEActiveCurrencyAndAmount_SimpleType` `pattern` regex, which was\n  over-escaped in YAML and failed to validate decimal monetary values.\n\n\n### v2.1.4\n\n* Changed PII Schema Objects to align with split domestic and international payment PII introduced to v2.1.\n\n### v2.1.3\n\n* Added `AccountId` to Account Opening operation responses\n\n### v2.1.2\n\n* Removed AccountNumber from `get /payment-consents/{ConsentId}/refund` SchemeName values.\n\n### v2.1.1\n\n* Added `emirates_id` to `DocumentEvidenceDetails`\n\n* Changed loan to finance for all Schema Objects names and object descriptions.\n\n* Changed CreditorReference and DebtorReference objects to remove pattern.\n\n* Changed CreditorReference, DebtorReference, and Reference objects to reduce maximum length to 35 characters.\n",
    "version": "v2.2.1"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://[Ozone_Connect_API]"
    }
  ],
  "source_path": "/payment-consents/{consentId}/refund",
  "operations": {
    "get": {
      "tags": [
        "Payments"
      ],
      "summary": "Retrieve Refund Account Details for a Payment Consent",
      "description": "Ozone can call this API from Financial Institutions to retrieve payment information.\n",
      "operationId": "getRefund",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/providerId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/aspspId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerOrgId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerClientId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerSoftwareStatementId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiUri"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiOperation"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/consentId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ozoneInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/psuIdentifier"
        },
        {
          "name": "consentId",
          "in": "path",
          "schema": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "required": true,
          "description": "Identifies the consent by an id\n"
        }
      ],
      "responses": {
        "200": {
          "description": "successful operation",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RefundGetResponse"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "400": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error400Response"
        },
        "403": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error403Response"
        },
        "500": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/error500Response"
        },
        "default": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/errorResponse"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "security": [
    {},
    {
      "OzoneConnectApiKey": []
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": [
        "placeholder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "securitySchemes": {
    "OzoneConnectApiKey": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using an API Key, which is a secret shared between the API Hub and the LFI.",
      "type": "apiKey",
      "in": "header",
      "name": "Authorization"
    },
    "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": {
      "type": "oauth2",
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Client Credentials grant type.\n\nLFIs must host an OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server to utilise this security pattern. Scope values are set during the onboarding process, and represented by a placeholder in this API description.\n",
      "flows": {
        "clientCredentials": {
          "tokenUrl": "https://example.lfi.ae/token",
          "scopes": {
            "placeholder": "Placeholder for scopes, which are set by the LFI during onboarding"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using the \"JWT Auth\" mechanism, where the Client presents a signed JSON Web Token as a credential.\n\nThe Server MUST verify the signature in order to authenticate the Client.\n\nPlease note that the value of the `scheme` parameter is not a registered HTTP Authentication Scheme, to indicate it is specific to Ozone Connect. Please refer to API Hub documentation for further details.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Ozone-Connect-JWT-Auth"
    },
    "OzoneConnectServiceInitiationToken": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Service Initiation Token.\n\nThe API Hub will set an Access Token based on a value set by the LFI, which has been patched onto the associated consent. The value will be transmitted in the `Authorization` header, which is represented as a `Bearer` in this Security Scheme Object.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Bearer"
    }
  }
}

{
  "name": "o3-provider-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "Identifier for the Financial Institution that the request is targeted to"
}

{
  "name": "o3-aspsp-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "deprecated": true,
  "description": "Identifier for the financial institution that the request is targeted to. This header is deprecated and will be removed in a future version of Ozone Connect. Use `o3-provider-id` instead."
}

